    "name": "The registry of known repositories",
    "line": "It holds the per-machine list of registered repositories, and decides which one a launch opens into.",
    "lines": 553,
    "bottom": true,
    "short": [
      "`ProjectRegistryStore` is an actor that owns the registry file in application support, and the only thing that writes it. A `ProjectRecord` has a stable id and a mutable path, so a directory that moves re-points the Project it already was. Each record carries at most one Binding per port."
    ],
    "long": [
      "`LaunchProject` decides where a launch points. An explicit override wins, then the active registered Project, then the directory the process started in. To point is not to register, because registration is a deliberate act rather than a side effect.",
      "A registry Argo cannot read is an empty one. A launch into an empty strip is recoverable, and a refusal to launch is not.",
      "`CockpitPointing` is the value the window strip draws from, and the value a gesture moves. Its acts describe a gesture, and a move says what the registry and the Hub must each do about it."
    ],
