      "It is an actor because the walk is disk work and its caller draws the caret. It caches nothing, because when to walk again belongs to the caller, which is the only place that knows the cost of a stale list.",
      "Argo reads plugins from the CLI's own record. `InstalledPlugins` decodes the installed-plugins file under the user's home, and `EnabledPlugins` reads the settings that say which of them are on.",
      "`SkillLoad` faces the other way. A transcript record names only a directory, so the reader opens the `SKILL.md` under it and returns what it found, or why it cannot. No code here calls into another group of the engine."
