    "name": "The overview lane",
    "line": "It draws the whole reading as a proportionate miniature, and maps a click back onto the scroll.",
    "lines": 2176,
    "bottom": true,
    "short": [
      "The lane is pinned to the feed it maps, and nothing comes between them. It takes the feed's table handle rather than the rows, because everything it draws is geometry the table already measured. A lane that sums anything else puts a rect where its row is not."
    ],
    "long": [
      "`MinimapGeometry` is the arithmetic. Row starts are a prefix sum, so a row's position is a lookup rather than a walk. The miniature is taller than the lane at any real Session length. Its scale comes from the widths, and not from what fits vertically. So the lane draws a window onto it.",
      "`MinimapGeometry` holds no scroll offset at all. Everything in it is still. The lane can freeze one geometry for a whole drag, and draw nothing again while the user scrolls.",
      "`MinimapLaneView` keeps the three things it draws on separate layers over the deck, because each of them changes on its own clock. The rects are a bitmap of one band, and Argo draws that band again only when its content changes. The viewport rectangle moves without a redraw of the rects. The annotations are the only layer a pointer moving over the lane touches."
    ],
